# Declared slow steps. Read by scripts/run-test-list.mjs: a step listed here gets 600 s instead of the 120 s every
# other step gets. A step here must also be on a gate list (test-list-completeness checks it).
# Keep it honest: add a step with its measured time from a full run (`--timings=<file>` writes them), and say why
# it is slow. A step that hangs is a bug to fix, not a step to list here.
#
# Measured on the full fast gate of 2026-10-27 (1425 steps in 25m33s on the Windows dev box, other sessions running).
# Every step at or over 40 s is listed, so a 2-3x slowdown under load cannot turn a healthy step red.
# qa-product-perfect-claims: clones the repo and inspects the claims authority — hit 120 s in the gate, 161 s standalone.
test/qa-product-perfect-claims.test.js
# stationbake.chunk: station bake chunking — 114.5 s.
test/stationbake.chunk.test.js
# cli-dashboard-drive: the real CLI dashboard driven by typed keys against a fake station — 87.7 s.
test/cli-dashboard-drive.test.js
# website-app-sync: runs scripts/sync-website-app.mjs --check over the whole frontend copy — 69.2 s.
test/website-app-sync.test.js
# ledger-reconcile: ends with a smoke of the real io shell against a throwaway git repo — 50.2 s.
test/ledger-reconcile.test.js
# browser: the browser automation contract suite — 42.6 s.
test/browser.test.js
# checkpoint-links: every row makes real shadow-git snapshots and rewinds over its own link fixtures — measured standalone
# on 2026-10-30 (lane checkpoint-links): 66 s at review 6.2, 79 s at final review 2; with the undo-closure rows
# (fr3-fr6: a capped runner, 60 and 120 entry budgets) 308 s, 461 s and 477 s while other gates held the CPU at 100%,
# near the 600 s limit: splitting row 20 into a file of its own is the follow-up if a gate cuts it off. Undo review 1's
# rows went to test/checkpoint-undo.test.js instead, so this file did not grow: 324 s and 187 s at that fix, other gates
# running (the first at 100% CPU). At undo review 2's fix (2026-10-30/31, other gates running): 121 s and 123 s at about
# 45% CPU, 163 s and 196 s at about 90%. At undo review 3's fix (2026-10-31, no new rows here): 123 s and 126 s at
# 40-57% CPU. At undo review 4's fix (2026-10-31, no new rows here): 150 s at 94% CPU, and 447 s in a run near 100%.
# At undo review 5's fix (2026-10-31, no new rows here; each rewind now lists both trees' modes once): 219 s at 66% CPU.
# Undo review 6 measured 323 s at 81% CPU, one row at a time. Since its fix the rows run four at a time, each on its
# own agent, and no Git starts a console host (test/helpers/checkpoint-rows.js). Measured standalone through
# scripts/run-test-list.mjs on 2026-11-01, the box rebooted at 12:49 that day: 41 s at 61% CPU and 48 s at 83%
# beside another gate, 130 s at 100% beside another; 132 s at 99% and 128 s at 100% with busy threads added; 92 s at 100%
# with 16 game instances and no gate, 91 s at 100% with 12-16 of them and the run queue at 45-81. ab10c33's file, one row
# at a time, that day: 142 s at 61%. Before that reboot, the box up since 2026-10-30 18:37 and a lone
# `git --version` taking 0.2-3 s to start and end (19-30 ms after it, 90-180 ms at 100% CPU): 141 s at 64% (2026-11-01
# 00:24); with a console host beside every Git (2026-10-31), 337 s at 94% and 381 s at 88%, cut off at 600 s once at 97%.
# At undo review 7's fix (2026-11-01 evening, no new rows here): 54 s at 76% and 77 s at 93% beside two other gates, 115 s
# at 100% with busy threads added. At undo review 8's fix (2026-11-02, no new rows here; one Git call more an operation, one
# more a rewind): 74 s at 50% and 54 s at 54% beside another lane's HTTP gate; 90 s and 88 s at 85-88% turn about with
# 2caa2665's file, which took 81 s and 94 s. Undo review 9 measured b5355821's file at 95-98% CPU, in the three rounds the
# checkpoint-undo entry names (2026-11-02 morning): 169 s, 212 s and 255 s. At its fix (no new rows here;
# a rewind's walk asks each folder it lists one lstat more): 61 s at 56% beside another session's fast gate, and 50 s at 37%
# turn about with b5355821's file, which took 59 s at 49%. Undo review 10 measured 37ab3794's file at 61.0 s at 50% and 84.2 s at
# 69%; at its fix (no new rows here): 76 s at 60% beside two other gates (2026-11-02). Undo review 11 measured d7247072's file at
# 83.2 s at 69%. At its fix (no new rows here, eight at a time, 2026-11-02 evening): 116 s at 90% turn about with d7247072's file, which
# took 170 s at 88%; 117 s at 84%, and 198 s at 87% with 8 game instances and a gate beside it.
test/checkpoint-links.test.js
